@description ReaWwise
@author Audiokinetic
@version 1.1.0
@changelog
  New Features
    - The About window now has an "Issues & Requests" link to ReaWwise's GitHub Issues page.
    - ReaWwise can import music objects, such as Music Segments, Music Tracks and, Music Playlist Containers when connected to Wwise 2024.1 or later.
    - You can now drag a resize bar to change the height of the "Wwise Structures" section relative to the rest of the window.
  API Changes
    - Building ReaWwise now requires the Wwise SDK 2023.1 or later. CMake configuration stops with an error if it finds an older SDK. Support code for earlier Wwise versions has been removed.
  Behavior Changes
    - In the import preview table, the status column headers now default to a third of the width of the other columns. This leaves more room for the object name columns.
    - There are now limits on log file size. Logged WAAPI arguments, options and results are now capped at 10,000 bytes each. Each log file is capped at 25 MB, and the oldest entries are removed past that. Log files older than 14 days are deleted at startup. The import preview now refreshes only when the import items or a watched property change. A WAV file modified outside the app shows up at the next such refresh, not on any REAPER change.
  Miscellaneous Changes
    - Fixed a problem that stopped ReaWwise from building on recent versions of macOS.
  Bug Fixes
    - Fixed: Korean text is not displayed correctly.
    - Fixed: Wwise Property Containers are sometimes inaccurately displayed in the Preview window. 
  Fixes for Community-Reported Bugs
    - Fixed: Nested Object creation does not apply the correct Object type to sub-folders.
@provides
  [win64] reaper_reawwise.dll https://github.com/audiokinetic/ReaWwise/releases/download/$version/reaper_reawwise.dll
  [darwin] reaper_reawwise.dylib https://github.com/audiokinetic/ReaWwise/releases/download/$version/reaper_reawwise.dylib
@screenshot User Interface https://github.com/audiokinetic/ReaWwise/blob/main/user-interface.png
@about
  # ReaWwise

  ReaWwise is a REAPER extension that sound designers can use to transfer audio files from REAPER into Wwise projects. The transfer process creates Wwise objects in manually defined hierarchies, so that Wwise users can start working with the imported sounds immediately.

  ### Supported Platforms
  - Windows
  - Mac

  ## Basic Usage
  1. Open your REAPER and Wwise projects.
  2. Configure your REAPER render settings appropriately. The render settings determine which files will be transferred to Wwise.
  3. Open ReaWwise and configure settings such as the Originals Subfolder (optional), Import Destination, Wwise Structures, and so on.
  4. Preview the audio files and Wwise objects to be transferred in the Preview Panel.
  4. Click **Transfer To Wwise** to transfer the audio files and create the corresponding Wwise objects.

  ## UserPlugins Directory
  - Windows:  %appdata%\REAPER\UserPlugins
  - Mac: ~/Library/Application Support/REAPER/UserPlugins

  ## Other Resources
  Refer to the [ReaWwise User Guide](https://audiokinetic.com/library/reawwise) for more information regarding usage, installation and troubleshooting of the extension.

  For general questions about usage, refer to Audiokinetic's [Community Q&A](https://www.audiokinetic.com/qa/ask).

  ## Contributing
  The repository is not open to pull request but in the case of a bug report, bugfix or a suggestions, please feel free to [open an issue](https://github.com/audiokinetic/ReaWwise/issues).

  Feature requests can also be submitted via the ["Ask a Question"](https://www.audiokinetic.com/qa/questions/reawwise) section using ReaWwise as the category.

